Looking at the comment: "If a set bit is found, all bits from fromIndex up to but not including the returned index are clear."

- "a set bit is found" → the return value is not -1 (`\result != -1`)
- "all bits from fromIndex up to but not including the returned index are clear" → for all `i` with `fromIndex <= i < \result`, `get(i)` is false.

<code>assert \result != -1 => \forall int i; fromIndex <= i && i < \result; !this.get(i);</code>
