Looking at the comment: "If a set bit is found, all bits from fromIndex up to but not including the returned index are clear."

A set bit is found when the method returns a valid index (not -1), i.e., `\result >= 0`. Then every bit `i` in the range `[fromIndex, \result)` must be clear (`!get(i)`).

<code>assert \result >= 0 => \forall int i; fromIndex <= i && i < \result; !this.get(i);</code>
